{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Lint Steering",
  "description": "Health-check + compression pass over steering: flag conflicts/drift/dead references, propose compressed rewrites of verbose steering, and prune decisions.md to short, high-impact entries.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Steering lint + compression pass. Operate terse: drop filler (just/really/basically/actually/simply), pleasantries, and hedging (might/perhaps/consider/it's worth noting); keep technical terms, identifiers, paths, and quoted errors exact; leave code blocks unchanged.\n\nRead every file in .kiro/steering/ AND .kiro/steering/decisions.md.\n\n## 1. Consistency check\nReport, grouped by category:\na. Steering rules that conflict with recent decisions.md entries.\nb. decisions.md entries not reflected in steering.\nc. Steering sections referencing removed code, dead patterns, or outdated file paths.\nd. Contradictions between steering files.\n\n## 2. Compress verbose steering (propose, don't apply blindly)\nFor each steering file note inclusion type + approx line count + density (verbose | moderate | already terse). Skip files already terse (<30 lines, mostly lists/code) and human-facing docs (READMEs). For verbose files, propose a compressed rewrite:\n- PRESERVE exactly: every rule/constraint/requirement, all code blocks/commands/paths/URLs, front-matter (inclusion/description/keywords), headings/lists/tables, technical terms.\n- REMOVE: filler, hedging, pleasantries, redundant restatement of headings, verbose transitions (\"In order to\", \"The reason for this is\"), unnecessary articles where meaning holds.\n- REWRITE: long sentences → short fragments where unambiguous; \"You should always make sure to X\" → \"Always X\"; passive → active where shorter.\nShow before/after line count per file. Rules preserved: all.\n\n## 3. Prune decisions.md\ndecisions.md is loaded into context, so it must stay short, concise, high-signal. For each entry decide KEEP / CONDENSE / DROP:\n- KEEP only entries with material impact on future work OR important historical record.\n- DROP entries that no longer affect anything (superseded, one-off already resolved with no lasting rule, obsolete).\n- CONDENSE survivors to the essential Problem/Decision/Rationale — cut re-verification narration, blow-by-blow logs, and duplicated detail. A survivor should be a few tight lines, not a story.\n- Flag duplicates/overlapping entries to merge.\nPropose the pruned result per entry (KEEP as-is | CONDENSE to: <text> | DROP because: <reason>).\n\n## Output\nApply nothing without showing proposed changes first. If everything is consistent, terse, and decisions.md is already lean, say 'Steering is consistent and lean.'"
  }
}